  "id": "empf-v2",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In empf-v1, flat soft Born-Infeld bounding (ebi_beta = 4.0) permitted critic slope drift across settled 8-mode equilibrium holds (mode_hold 5/8 modes), while unconditioned discrete-simplex couplings kept DualNorm uncooled forever after joint BiGAN convergence so a borderline word bounced across a logit boundary during multi-thousand-step holds (five_word_joint_hold 24/25 checks). Starting at ebi_beta = 6.0 preserves 16-mode spreading during acquisition while sharpening the Born-Infeld barrier once e-means transport residual settles (ema_residual < 0.16) in proportion to prototype-bank batch resolution, and Sinkhorn-residual-driven post-acquisition thermal cooling stabilizes converged discrete-simplex boundaries without slowing initial acquisition.",
